## 8. Memory View

Memory View is used to analyze the memory usage of a Flutter application.

It helps identify memory-related problems such as memory leaks and unnecessary object creation.

### Features

- Displays memory usage.
- Tracks memory allocation.
- Monitors garbage collection (GC).
- Helps identify memory leaks.
- Provides heap snapshots for analyzing objects.

### Example

Suppose an application continuously creates objects without releasing references to them.

This may cause memory usage to increase continuously.

Using Memory View, developers can monitor memory allocation and identify objects that remain in memory unnecessarily.

Use: Memory View is useful for improving application stability and preventing excessive memory consumption.&#x20;

