## 11. Flutter Error and Exception Debugging

Flutter provides error-handling mechanisms to identify errors during application execution.

### Common errors

| Error                                    | Meaning                                      |
| ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| RenderFlex overflow                      | A Row or Column exceeds available space      |
| Null check operator used on a null value | A null value was accessed using `!`          |
| Incorrect use of ParentDataWidget        | A widget is used in an invalid parent layout |
| Unbounded constraints                    | A widget receives infinite constraints       |
| Exception                                | An unexpected runtime problem occurs         |

### Example: RenderFlex overflow

```
Row(
  children: [
    Container(width: 200),
    Container(width: 200),
    Container(width: 200),
  ],
)
```

If the screen width is smaller than the total width of the children, the Row may overflow.

The Flutter console displays an error message.

Possible solutions:

- Use `Expanded`.
- Use `Flexible`.
- Use a `SingleChildScrollView`.
- Adjust the width of the widgets.

This is a common UI debugging problem in Flutter.&#x20;

