## 12. Debug Mode, Profile Mode, and Release Mode

Flutter supports three main execution modes.

| Mode         | Purpose                            |
| ------------ | ---------------------------------- |
| Debug Mode   | Used for development and debugging |
| Profile Mode | Used for performance analysis      |
| Release Mode | Used for production deployment     |

### Debug Mode

- Supports breakpoints.
- Supports hot reload.
- Provides detailed error messages.
- Enables debugging tools.

Command:

```
flutter run
```

### Profile Mode

Used to analyze performance on a device with optimizations enabled.

```
flutter run --profile
```

### Release Mode

Used to run the optimized application for production.

```
flutter run --release
```

Note: Debugging features such as breakpoints and most debug-only visualizations are not available in release mode.&#x20;

